\", \"static_checks\": [\"grep-verified no tl.range remains in kernel bodies; all inner k-loops now plain range(); num_stages=2 on all four launches\"], \"notes\": \"REFUTED: tl.range/num_stages was not the cause; identical uniform RUNTIME_ERROR persists. Cleared surfaces so far: erf/libdevice (c002), broadcast rank (c003), loop-pipelining (c004). Remaining live single-surface suspects: (a) the tl.dot CALL CONVENTION `tl.dot(a,w,out_dtype=tl.float32)` in conv2/conv3/linear -- switch to the canonical 3-arg accumulate form `acc = tl.dot(a,w,acc)` (tutorial-exact, no out_dtype kwarg); (b) conv1_kernel itself (unchanged since c001) or run()-setup asserts. Next c005: switch all three dots to the accumulate form. If still RUNTIME_ERROR, the dot convention is cleared and the following candidate will target conv1/run() directly (e.g., a diagnostic that isolates whether conv1 alone executes).\"}\n{\"candidate_id\": \"c005\", \"candidate\": \"c005\", \"parent\": \"c004\", \"source_sha256\": \"57b1f16f1e80e2bdca7d2dbb5badd647e23b5f1b699006871a09cac8a36ba08a\", \"phase\": \"feedback\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-17T21:12:24Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"The uniform RUNTIME_ERROR is a Triton compile error at the tl.dot call convention. All three dot kernels used `acc += tl.dot(a, w, out_dtype=tl.float32)`; the `out_dtype=` kwarg is version-fragile. Switch every call to the tutorial-exact 3-arg accumulate form `acc = tl.dot(a, w, acc)` (fp32 accumulator carried in positionally, no out_dtype kwarg). Semantically identical fp32 accumulation.\", \"change_from_parent\": \"All three `acc += tl.dot(a, w, out_dtype=tl.float32)` (conv2/conv3/linear) -> `acc = tl.dot(a, w, acc)`. No other changes.\", \"changes_vs_parent\": \"tl.dot call convention only (out_dtype kwarg -> 3-arg accumulate form).\", \"validation\": {\"structural_guards\": \"pass\", \"all_workloads_pass\": false, \"per_workload\": [{\"wl\": \"w1\", \"uuid\": \"9415ba43-1612-5a34-a400-0e351edb434e\", \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"p